is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: The access interface facing the host subnet on leaf_router_0_0 (interface eth2, gateway IP 10.0.0.1/24) is down.

Mechanism: pc_0_0 cannot ARP for its default gateway. On pc_0_0, “ip neigh” shows 10.0.0.1 FAILED and pings to 10.0.0.1 return “Destination Host Unreachable.” pc_0_0’s NIC is up but receives nothing (RX 0), so ARP requests get no reply. On the leaf, the gateway interface is not operational, so it cannot send ARP replies or forward traffic.

Localization: On leaf_router_0_0, eth2 is administratively down: ip addr shows eth2 state DOWN with 10.0.0.1/24 configured; ethtool reports “Link detected: no,” and ifconfig lacks UP/RUNNING flags with zero TX/RX (and drops). Conversely, the fabric core is healthy: leaf_router_0_0 can reach spine_router_0_0 (ping 172.16.0.4 succeeds), and it has a BGP-learned route to 10.0.1.0/24. On the other leaf (leaf_router_0_1), the host-facing eth2 is UP and reachable from pc_0_1.

Root cause: Interface eth2 on leaf_router_0_0 (the default gateway for 10.0.0.0/24) is administratively down/has no link, isolating pc_0_0’s subnet from the fabric.

Corrective fix: Do not replace spine_router_0_0. Instead, bring up or bounce the host-facing port on leaf_router_0_0: “ip link set dev eth2 up” (or restart the interface). After eth2 is UP/RUNNING with link detected, pc_0_0 will ARP successfully for 10.0.0.1 and regain connectivity across the fabric.
=== END ===